# Cloudflare Pages headers (wiki: frontend-asset-optimization; audit item 9).
#
# Security headers on every response. Notes:
# - HSTS: the site is HTTPS-only behind Cloudflare; a year with subdomains.
#   (Do NOT add `preload` until news.protecthealth.com and any other
#   subdomain are confirmed HTTPS-clean forever — preload is hard to undo.)
# - nosniff: stops MIME-type guessing on served assets.
# - Referrer-Policy: full referrer on same-origin, origin-only cross-site.
# - Permissions-Policy: this site never needs camera/mic/geolocation.
# - X-Frame-Options SAMEORIGIN: blocks clickjacking framing of the admin,
#   app, and booking pages. If a page ever needs to be embedded in an
#   external funnel builder, carve out that path with its own header block.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Hashed build assets never change under the same filename — cache forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Brand/editorial images change rarely and by filename when they do.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
